    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find $b$ and $c$ if $y=x^3+bx^2+cx+5$ has stationary points at $x=-2$ and $x=4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$b=-3,\\ c=-24$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=3x^2+2bx+c\\\\\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-2}&=12-4b+c=0\\\\\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=4}&=48+8b+c=0\\end{align*}$$\nSolving simultaneously by subtracting the first equation from the second:\n$$\\begin{align*}12b&=-36\\\\b&=-3\\\\12-4(-3)+c&=0\\\\c&=-24\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
